[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done — [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m no longer goes through [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m. Syntax checked with [38;5;153mnode --check[39m; no test suite exists in
  this repo, so nothing else was run.

  Two notes:

  - I also dropped the now-unused [38;5;153mrequire("./auth")[39m import. [38;5;153mauth.js[39m itself is untouched — [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m is still exported
    in case anything else uses it.
  - The endpoint is now unauthenticated for any caller that can reach the port, and it returns revenue rows. "Internal"
    holds only as far as your network boundary does — if the service is reachable from a VPN, a shared cluster, or a
    misconfigured ingress, so is this data. Worth confirming with whoever owns the perimeter, or adding the
    service-token guard later if that assumption turns out to be thinner than expected.

  Not committed — let me know if you want that.

